        "name": "USN-5378-3",
        "description": "USN-5378-2 fixed a vulnerability in XZ Utils. This update provides the corresponding update for Ubuntu 14.04 ESM and 16.04 ESM.  Original advisory details:   Cleemy Desu Wayo discovered that Gzip incorrectly handled certain  filenames. If a user or automated system were tricked into performing zgrep  operations with specially crafted filenames, a remote attacker could  overwrite arbitrary files.",
